WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.394 --> 00:00:08.405
Imagine Alice has an idea

00:00:08.405 --> 00:00:10.190
and she wants to share it.

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:13.313
There are so many ways to share an idea.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.321
She could draw a picture,
make an engraving,

00:00:15.321 --> 00:00:16.708
write a song.

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:19.172
(piano playing)

00:00:24.777 --> 00:00:26.326
(pounding)

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.851
send a telegraph,

00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:29.118
(wire clicking)

00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:31.450
or an email.

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:33.998
But how are these things different?

00:00:34.846 --> 00:00:36.264
And more importantly,

00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:38.232
why are they the same?

00:00:42.497 --> 00:00:44.997
This story is about the
fundamental particle

00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:47.129
of all forms of communication.

00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:50.271
It begins with a special skill

00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:52.083
you likely take for granted,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.553
language.

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:57.627
All language allows you to
take thought or mental object

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.156
and break it down into a
series of conceptual chunks.

00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:04.242
These chunks are externalized

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:07.160
using a series signals or symbols.

00:01:07.796 --> 00:01:10.116
Humans express themselves
using a variation

00:01:10.116 --> 00:01:12.242
in sound and physical action.

00:01:14.102 --> 00:01:17.523
As do chirping birds and dancing bees,

00:01:18.394 --> 00:01:21.303
and man-made machines
exchanging a dancing stream

00:01:21.303 --> 00:01:23.171
of electrical vibrations.

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.315
Even our bodies are built
according to instructions

00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:30.989
stored inside microscopic
books known as DNA.

00:01:31.272 --> 00:01:33.794
All are different forms of one thing:

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.890
Information.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.254
In simplest terms,

00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:40.857
information is what allows
one mind to influence another.

00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:45.312
It's based on the idea of
communication as selection.

00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:48.001
Information, no matter the form,

00:01:48.001 --> 00:01:50.397
can be measured using a fundamental unit.

00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:53.654
In the same way we can measure
the mass of different objects

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.809
using a standard measure
such as kilograms or pounds,

00:01:57.197 --> 00:01:59.585
this allows us to precisely
measure and compare

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:02.661
the weight of say rocks, water, or wheat,

00:02:02.781 --> 00:02:04.497
using a scale.

00:02:06.175 --> 00:02:08.684
Information, too, can
be measured and compared

00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:11.332
using a measurement called entropy.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.328
Think of it as an information scale.

00:02:14.711 --> 00:02:16.879
We intuitively know that a single page

00:02:16.879 --> 00:02:19.332
from some unknown book
has less information

00:02:19.978 --> 00:02:22.042
than the entire book.

00:02:22.454 --> 00:02:24.516
We can describe exactly how much

00:02:24.516 --> 00:02:26.848
using a unit called the bit.

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:29.056
A measure of surprise.

00:02:29.472 --> 00:02:31.133
So no matter how Alice wants

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.088
to communicate a specific message,

00:02:33.547 --> 00:02:34.700
hieroglyphics,

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.949
music,

00:02:36.244 --> 00:02:37.436
computer code,

00:02:37.848 --> 00:02:40.452
each would contain the
same number of bits,

00:02:40.677 --> 00:02:42.359
though in different densities,

00:02:42.811 --> 00:02:45.912
and a bit is linked to a very simple idea.

00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:49.763
The answer to a yes or no question.

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:52.187
Think of it as the language of coins.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.316
So how is information actually measured?

00:02:55.528 --> 00:02:57.519
Does information have a speed limit?

00:02:57.896 --> 00:02:59.683
A maximum density?

00:02:59.786 --> 00:03:02.471
Information theory hold
the exciting answer

00:03:02.471 --> 00:03:04.062
to these questions.

00:03:04.429 --> 00:03:06.896
It's an idea over 3,000
years in the making,

00:03:08.161 --> 00:03:10.061
but before we can understand this,

00:03:10.061 --> 00:03:12.408
we must step back and explore, perhaps,

00:03:12.408 --> 00:03:15.519
the most powerful
invention in human history.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.944
The alphabet.

00:03:17.337 --> 00:03:20.069
And for this, we return to the cave.

